msgid "demo.component.input"
msgstr "Input source. Edit values directly: 0–15 for 4 bits; 0–1 for 1 bit."

msgid "demo.component.output"
msgstr "Observer: displays the connected value without changing it."

msgid "demo.component.mux2_word"
msgstr "Two-way selector: SEL=0 outputs A; SEL=1 outputs B. Data is 4 bits; select is 1 bit."

msgid "demo.component.register4"
msgstr "At a step boundary, LOAD=1 saves DATA; LOAD=0 holds Q. Initial value is 0."

msgid "demo.component.ram2x4"
msgstr "Two independent 4-bit locations. ADDR selects 0/1; WRITE=1 stores DATA_IN at a step boundary. DATA_OUT reads the selected location."

msgid "demo.task.dp_select.title"
msgstr "P-1 Connect your first machine"

msgid "demo.task.dp_select.goal"
msgstr "Use SEL to choose the value from A or B and send it to OUT."

msgid "demo.task.dp_select.specs"
msgstr "MUX: SEL=0 → A; SEL=1 → B. Example: A=3, B=9, SEL=1 must output 9.\nData ports are 4-bit; control is 1-bit. Connections are limited only by direction and width.\nDrag ports to wire; drag an input connection away to disconnect. Undo is available above. Edit input numbers to inspect output. Run validates all 512 input combinations."

msgid "demo.task.dp_select.hint1"
msgstr "Consider how the two data sources enter the selector."

msgid "demo.task.dp_select.hint2"
msgstr "Data and select have different roles; OUT needs the selected value."

msgid "demo.task.dp_select.hint3"
msgstr "Reference wiring, read only: A→MUX.A, B→MUX.B, SEL→MUX.SEL, MUX.Y→OUT."

msgid "demo.task.dp_store.title"
msgstr "P-2 Keep the result"

msgid "demo.task.dp_store.goal"
msgstr "Save a value, keep two values at independent addresses, then retrieve them with LOAD/STORE."

msgid "demo.task.dp_store.specs"
msgstr "All stored values start at 0. Input preview does not write; Step commits once. Run verifies independent sequences.\nDATA/Q are 4-bit values; LOAD, ADDR and WRITE are 1-bit controls.\nAccepted earlier circuits remain saved; Continue adds the next components."

msgid "demo.task.dp_store.hint1"
msgstr "Observe which stored value should change on write and remain on hold."

msgid "demo.task.dp_store.hint2"
msgstr "A register receives a value; RAM also needs an address. A LOAD must actually route RAM data back into the register."

msgid "demo.task.dp_store.hint3"
msgstr "Reference only: stage A DATA→REG.DATA, LOAD→REG.LOAD, REG.Q→Q. Stage B ADDR/WRITE/DATA→RAM corresponding ports, RAM.DATA_OUT→MEM. Stage C DATA/RAM→SOURCE.A/B, READ→SOURCE.SEL, SOURCE.Y→REG.DATA, REG.Q→RAM.DATA_IN."

msgid "demo.task.d1_upgrade.title"
msgstr "1-2 Where should the upgrade go?"

msgid "demo.task.d1_upgrade.goal"
msgstr "Replace only one part per scenario. Preserve outputs: scenario A ≤100 cycles; scenario B ≤96 cycles."

msgid "demo.task.d1_upgrade.specs"
msgstr "Compare CPU, RAM and Bus upgrades. Continue to the second scenario after completing the first.\nDrawing distance has no timing cost. RAM service and bus transfer are distinct events included in wait along with control.\nCost is shown separately; keep comparing after completion."

msgid "demo.task.d1_upgrade.hint1"
msgstr "Compare cycles spent computing, servicing RAM and transferring."

msgid "demo.task.d1_upgrade.hint2"
msgstr "A faster part only shortens the work it owns."

msgid "demo.task.d1_upgrade.hint3"
msgstr "Reference direction: reduce RAM service cycles in A; increase bus bits per cycle in B."

msgid "demo.task.d2_cache.title"
msgstr "2-1 Stop making distant trips"

msgid "demo.task.d2_cache.goal"
msgstr "Repeated reads slow the job. Enable one cache line and reuse data after the first fetch."

msgid "demo.task.d2_cache.specs"
msgstr "Program and capacity are fixed. Cache is hardware-managed.\nA is stored by row; one line fetches 4 integers. A missing line needs RAM; resident data can hit.\nNear means lower access cost, not screen distance. Complete with correct output and actual misses followed by hits."

msgid "demo.task.d2_cache.hint1"
msgstr "Inspect how much data one RAM fetch returns."

msgid "demo.task.d2_cache.hint2"
msgstr "A fetched line can serve later requests."

msgid "demo.task.d2_cache.hint3"
msgstr "Reference action: enable the one-line cache and run."

msgid "demo.task.d2_group.title"
msgstr "2-3 Finish this small block first"

msgid "demo.task.d2_group.goal"
msgstr "Process the same data in two independent passes. Keep one cache line and schedule groups. Preserve each pass sum and reach ≤145 cycles."

msgid "demo.task.d2_group.specs"
msgstr "Each independent pass stores its own sum; the results are not added together. Read every element exactly once per pass.\nNo cross-group dependencies: both passes for one group may finish first. Program and cache stay fixed.\nCompare actual event groups, passes and cache residency."

msgid "demo.task.d2_group.hint1"
msgstr "After leaving this data, will it still be resident when you return?"

msgid "demo.task.d2_group.hint2"
msgstr "One cache line can retain 4 consecutive elements. Change the reuse interval between passes."

msgid "demo.task.d2_group.hint3"
msgstr "Reference schedule: 1 line per group, finish both passes before moving on."

msgid "demo.task.d2_final.title"
msgstr "2-4 The final job"

msgid "demo.task.d2_final.goal"
msgstr "Two-pass processing: change program, cache size and grouping. Preserve each pass result and workload; reach ≤145 cycles. Optional goal: cost ≤4."

msgid "demo.task.d2_final.specs"
msgstr "Start with two cache lines; change multiple settings together. Specifications and run evidence are always available.\nEach pass reads all 16 elements and stores its own sum; each run starts cold. Grouping uses the same independent-pass contract as the previous task.\nCompare speed and cost separately, and keep exploring cheaper solutions after completion."

msgid "demo.task.d2_final.hint1"
msgstr "Experiment with one idea: retain more data, or reuse it sooner."

msgid "demo.task.d2_final.hint2"
msgstr "Several changes can work together, but the comparison cannot attribute the result to one of them alone."

msgid "demo.task.d2_final.hint3"
msgstr "Two reference directions, read only: 4 cache lines with whole-table passes; or 1 cache line with 1-line groups and both passes per group. They can be equally fast at different costs."

msgid "demo.task.dp_store.stage0"
msgstr "A · LOAD=1 writes DATA; LOAD=0 holds Q. Connect the register and observer."

msgid "demo.task.dp_store.stage1"
msgstr "B · Add two addresses. ADDR selects 0/1; WRITE=1 stores DATA on Step. Keep the register path from stage A."

msgid "demo.task.dp_store.stage2"
msgstr "C · Data must travel between register and RAM. The two direct DATA wires have been removed; the accepted prior design remains saved.\nSOURCE chooses DATA or the RAM return; READ=1 selects RAM.\nSequence: set value → STORE address0 → set other value → STORE address1 → LOAD address0 → LOAD address1. LOAD=1 commits the register; WRITE=1 commits RAM."

msgid "demo.task.d1_upgrade.stage0"
msgstr "Scenario A: sum task with initial RAM service of 12 cycles per request. Target ≤100 cycles."

msgid "demo.task.d1_upgrade.stage1"
msgstr "Scenario B: copy task; RAM service is 4 cycles, but Bus transfers only 2 bits per cycle. Target ≤96 cycles."

